Subject: Skip deliberate OOB memcpy/MAP_FIXED VMA sub-test in tests/test-free.c under Fil-C
Policy-Class: P2-Package
Rationale: The Linux VMA-exhaustion sub-test in gnulib tests/test-free.c allocates malloc(big_size - 0x100) and intentionally reads 0x100 bytes out of bounds via memcpy() before calling MAP_FIXED mmap(). Upstream already skips this sub-test under __SANITIZE_ADDRESS__ because it triggers a heap-buffer-overflow trap; Fil-C's capability bounds check catches the exact same OOB access. All four real free() errno-preservation sub-tests (NULL, small, medium, large allocations) remain active.
Upstream-Status: Pending
Fil-C-Origin-Commits: original

diff --git a/tests/test-free.c b/tests/test-free.c
--- a/tests/test-free.c
+++ b/tests/test-free.c
@@ -92,7 +92,7 @@
 
   /* Skip this test when an address sanitizer is in use, because it would report
      a "heap buffer overflow".  */
-  #ifndef __SANITIZE_ADDRESS__
+  #if !defined __SANITIZE_ADDRESS__ && !defined __FILC__
   /* Test a less common code path.
      When malloc() is based on mmap(), free() can sometimes call munmap().
      munmap() usually succeeds, but fails in a particular situation: when
